Frontend Assessment
HTML & CSS Only (NO JavaScript)
Project: Grocery E-Commerce Website (Single Home Page)
Objective
Students must build a single-page grocery e-commerce website using only HTML5 and CSS3.
 The design should be inspired by the home page layout of Amazon or Flipkart, but must not be copied.
Technology Constraints
Only HTML5 and CSS3 are allowed
JavaScript is strictly not allowed
No frameworks or libraries (Bootstrap, Tailwind, React, etc.)
No backend
One page only (index.html)
Folder Structure (Mandatory)

grocery-assessment/
│── index.html
│── style.css
│── images/

Required Sections
1. Header / Navbar
The navigation bar must include:
• Grocery store logo (text or image)
• Search bar (UI only, no functionality)
• Navigation links:
Home
Categories
Offers
Cart
CSS expectations:
Flexbox for layout
Proper alignment and spacing
Hover effects on links
Sticky navbar is optional


2. Hero Section
A large banner section at the top of the page:
Background image or gradient
Main heading
Short description
“Shop Now” button (UI only)
CSS expectations:
Background positioning
Button hover transitions
Clean typography

3. Categories Section
Display at least 5 grocery categories, such as:
Fruits & Vegetables
Dairy Products
Snacks
Beverages
Household Items
CSS expectations:
CSS Grid layout
Card-based design
Hover effects on cards

4. Featured Products Section
Product cards must include:
Product image
Product name
Price
“Add to Cart” button (visual only)
CSS expectations:
Consistent card design
Box-shadow and hover animation
Proper spacing and alignment

5. Offers / Deals Section
A promotional section displaying:
Discount banners or offer cards
Highlighted text for deals
CSS expectations:
Good color contrast
Clear section separation

6. Footer
Footer must include:
Store description
Contact information
Copyright text
CSS expectations:
Clean layout
Readable text hierarchy
Responsiveness (Mandatory)
Mobile view: stacked layout
Tablet view: adjusted grid
Desktop view: full layout
Media queries must be used
Design Guidelines
Use Flexbox and Grid properly
Maintain consistent colors and fonts
Professional grocery store look
Clean and organized CSS